  "note": "Third annual election (five seats), Tuesday 15 January 1901, for the places of the members retiring by rotation (Gilchrist, Clarke, Fleming, M'Caughey and M'Neice). Eleven nominations were received by 5 p.m. on Saturday 5 January (Joseph Lunn and Murtagh M'Cann were nominated but are not in the result). \"Of the 2,096 electors on the register 1,077 exercised the franchise\", with two spoiled votes (the figure 2,096 is as printed; 2,606 were on the register in 1900). The Lurgan Mail prints surnames only in the result; Douie is printed \"Dowie\". No party labels printed."
